repository-code: "https://github.com/JoukeVerlinden/relightcam-ios"
url: "https://github.com/JoukeVerlinden/relightcam-ios/tree/relightcam/ios"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  relightCam captures relightable images (RTI, reflectance transformation imaging) with an iPhone and
  processes them on the phone: light directions from the highlight on a reflective sphere, or from the
  calibrated LEDs of a light dome that the app drives over USB MIDI, and a PTM or HSH fit written in the
  web format of the relight toolkit (CNR-ISTI Visual Computing Lab). The result can be explored in a 2D
  viewer, draped on a simulated 3D cloth (board, historical dress forms, free cloth) and shown in AR, and
  exported for OpenLIME and RelightLab. It is aimed at the documentation of textiles and other flat objects
  in cultural heritage and design education. The app lives in the ios/ folder of this fork of relight;
  everything outside ios/ is the upstream relight toolkit by CNR-ISTI. The ios/dome/ folder holds the
  Arduino sketch for the dome controller and a patch that adds USB MIDI to the Arduino UNO R4 core.
keywords:
  - reflectance transformation imaging
  - RTI
  - polynomial texture maps
  - hemispherical harmonics
  - cultural heritage
  - textiles
  - light dome
  - iOS
